    "authoredFrom": "Read from the case's input bytes: grund.toml (version 1, strict, `{kind}-{slug}` with `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*` slugs, named sections, `[scan] include = [\"docs\"]`, cross-refs off) and docs/ holding FS-c, FS-login with its named section `requirements`, FS-log, and cites.md. Lines 3-7 of cites.md are marked candidates holding a glob operator that are neither declared nor grammatical, so each is a pattern recording no citation and one glob-citation warning at its marker (§FS-citations.recognized.globs, §FS-check.checks.glob-citation); the emphasis, question, footnote, trailing-star and bold forms on lines 8-12 stay citations of FS-login and FS-c (§FS-check.1.1.11), and line 13 is escaped. FS-log is therefore never cited (§FS-check.4.1). The FS home is docs/functional-spec, which holds none of these files, so no index is owed (§FS-check.3.18), and with cross-refs off a plain `fmt` has nothing to do while `fmt --write --cross-refs` wraps the five citations to their headings, the emphasis, punctuation and footnote left outside each link (§FS-fmt.6.7.2, §FS-fmt.6.2). The editor carries each glob finding over its candidate (§FS-check.checks.glob-citation).",
